[{"text":"அல்குல்","lemma":"alkul","gloss":"loins / waist"}],"gloss":"loins"},{"surface":"தாங்கா","parts":[{"text":"தாங்கா","lemma":"tāṅku","gloss":"not bearing"}],"gloss":"not bearing"},{"surface":"அசைஇ","parts":[{"text":"அசைஇ","lemma":"acai","gloss":"having swayed"}],"gloss":"having swayed"},{"surface":"மெல்லென","parts":[{"text":"மெல்","lemma":"mel","gloss":"gentle"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"gently"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கலங்கலந்","parts":[{"text":"கலங்கலந்","lemma":"கலங்கலந்","gloss":"mixed"}],"gloss":"mixed","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தேறல்","parts":[{"text":"தேறல்","lemma":"tēṟal","gloss":"clear liquor"}],"gloss":"clear liquor"},{"surface":"பொலங்கலத்து","parts":[{"text":"பொலங்கலத்து","lemma":"பொலங்கலத்து","gloss":"in golden vessel"}],"gloss":"in golden vessel","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஏந்தி","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்தி","lemma":"ēnti","gloss":"holding"}],"gloss":"holding"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அமிழ்தென","parts":[{"text":"அமிழ்து","lemma":"amiḻtu","gloss":"nectar"},{"text":"என","lemma":"eṉa","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like nectar"},{"surface":"மடுப்ப","parts":[{"text":"மடுப்ப","lemma":"maṭu","gloss":"to feed / pour"}],"gloss":"to pour"},{"surface":"மாந்தி","parts":[{"text":"மாந்தி","lemma":"mānti","gloss":"having drunk"}],"gloss":"having drunk"},{"surface":"இகழ்விலன்","parts":[{"text":"இகழ்வு","lemma":"ikaḻvu","gloss":"negligence / fault"},{"text":"இலன்","lemma":"ilaṉ","gloss":"he is without"}],"gloss":"he is without negligence"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நில்லா","parts":[{"text":"நில்லா","lemma":"nillā","gloss":"unstable / transient"}],"gloss":"unstable"},{"surface":"உலகத்து","parts":[{"text":"உலகத்து","lemma":"ulakam","gloss":"of the world"}],"gloss":"of the world"},{"surface":"நிலையாமைநீ","parts":[{"text":"நிலையாமை","lemma":"nilaiyāmai","gloss":"impermanence"},{"text":"நீ","lemma":"nī","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"impermanence, you"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சொல்லா","parts":[{"text":"சொல்லா","lemma":"சொல்லா","gloss":"to say"}],"gloss":"to say","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வேண்டா","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டா","lemma":"vēṇṭā","gloss":"not needed"}],"gloss":"need not"},{"surface":"தோன்றல்","parts":[{"text":"தோன்றல்","lemma":"tōṉṟal","gloss":"lord / king"}],"gloss":"the lord"},{"surface":"முந்துஅறிந்த","parts":[{"text":"முந்து","lemma":"muntu","gloss":"beforehand"},{"text":"அறிந்த","lemma":"ari","gloss":"knew"}],"gloss":"already knew beforehand"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"முழுதுஉணர்","parts":[{"text":"முழுது","lemma":"muḻutu","gloss":"completely"},{"text":"உணர்","lemma":"uṇar","gloss":"understanding"}],"gloss":"completely understanding"},{"surface":"கேள்வியன்","parts":[{"text":"கேள்வியன்","lemma":"kēḷviyaṉ","gloss":"man of learning"}],"gloss":"man of learning"},{"surface":"ஆகலின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகலின்","lemma":"ākaliṉ","gloss":"since he is"}],"gloss":"since he is"},{"surface":"விரகினானே","parts":[{"text":"விரகினான்","lemma":"virakiṉāṉ","gloss":"man of wisdom"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"with wisdom indeed"}]}],"literal":"The singer, the subject, the landscape, and the theme are not known. / Roaring like thunder that opposes the rainy season, with a loud noise, / insatiable Death that causes precious life to suffer, / he does not fear your arrival indeed! Many good / sacrificial Brahmins who have completed their learning, / scattering rare ornaments with water, with great dignity, / more kindly than a mother, giving to many, / with dark male elephants of disciplined gait, his / grace having well bestowed on those who sing, / killing enemies with many chariots of rolling movement, his / sweetly giving to those who seek refuge at his feet, / to the songstress wearing twisted garlands, / with the bards wearing golden lotus flowers, / with long, dark hands that embraced them together, / with patience filled with chastity, of deer-like glance, / with eyebrows curved like bows, quickly / whose tongues fear when they speak, women of thorn-like teeth, / moving gently, unable to bear their heavy loins, / holding clear liquor in golden vessels, / drinking it as if it were nectar, without negligence, / the impermanence of this unstable world, you / need not tell him! The lord already knew this beforehand, / since he is a man of complete understanding and learning, with wisdom.","translation":"The poet, the subject, the landscape, and the theme of this poem are unknown. O insatiable Death, who roars with a loud noise like thunder in the rainy season and makes precious lives tremble! He does not fear your arrival at all. For he has already given away rare ornaments with water to Brahmins of complete learning who perform sacrifices, with a kindness greater than a mother's. He has bestowed his grace and dark elephants of disciplined gait upon those who sing of him. He has destroyed enemies with many rolling chariots and sweetly given refuge to those who sought his feet. With his long, dark hands, he has embraced the songstress wearing twisted garlands and the bards wearing golden lotuses. He has enjoyed the company of women with deer-like glances, patient chastity, bow-curved eyebrows, and sharp, thorn-like teeth, whose tongues hesitate out of modesty when they speak. As they swayed gently, unable to bear their heavy loins, and offered clear liquor in golden vessels, he drank it like nectar, never losing his dignity. Therefore, you do not need to lecture him on the impermanence of this fleeting world! Our lord already knew this beforehand, for he is a man of complete learning and profound wisdom.","modern":"இப்பாடலின் பாடியவர், பாடப்பட்டவர், திணை, துறை ஆகியவை அறியப்படவில்லை. கார் காலத்து இடி முழக்கம் போல உரக்க ஒலித்து, அரிய உயிர்களை நடுங்கச் செய்யும் பசியடங்காத கூற்றுவனே! அவன் உனது வருகையைக் கண்டு அஞ்சமாட்டான். ஏனெனில், அவன் கேள்வி அறிவு மிக்க வேள்வி செய்யும் அந்தணர்களுக்குத் தாயை விடவும் மேலாக இரங்கி, நீரோடு அரிய அணிகலன்களை வாரி வழங்கியவன். தன்னைப் பாடும் பாணர்களுக்கு ஒழுங்கான நடையையுடைய பெரிய ஆண் யானைகளை வழங்கி அருள் புரிந்தவன். உருண்டோடும் பல தேர்களைக் கொண்ட பகைவர்களை அழித்து, தன் அடி பணிந்தவர்களுக்கு இனிய கொடைகளை நல்கியவன். முறுக்கிய மாலைகளை அணிந்த பாடினிக்கும், பொன்னாலான தாமரை மலர்களை அணிந்த பாணர்களுக்கும் தன் நீண்ட கைகளால் அணைத்து ஆதரவு தந்தவன். பொறுமையும் கற்பும் மானைப் போன்ற பார்வையும் கொண்ட, வில் போன்ற புருவங்களையும் முள் போன்ற பற்களையும் உடைய, பேசும் போது நாணத்தால் நா அஞ்சும் மகளிர், தம் அல்குல் பாரம் தாங்காமல் மெல்ல அசைந்து வந்து, பொற்கலத்தில் தெளிந்த கள்ளினை அமிழ்தம் போல ஊட்ட, அதனைப் பருகி மகிழ்ந்தவன். இத்தகைய பெருமைகளைக் கொண்ட நம் தலைவனுக்கு, இந்த நிலையற்ற உலகத்தின் நிலையாமையைப் பற்றி நீ அறிவுறுத்த வேண்டியதில்லை. அவன் ஏற்கனவே முழுமையான கேள்வி அறிவும் பேரறிவும் கொண்டவனாக இருப்பதால், இதனை நன்கு உணர்ந்தவனே ஆவான்.","explanation":"This poem is addressed directly to Death (Yama), personified as an insatiable force that terrifies living beings. The poet boldly asserts that the great king does not fear Death's arrival because he has lived a complete, virtuous, and generous life. He has fulfilled all his duties: giving lavishly to learned Brahmins, patronizing bards and songstresses, defeating enemies, and protecting refugees. He has also fully enjoyed the pleasures of life, drinking clear liquor served by beautiful women, yet always maintaining his dignity and self-control. Therefore, the poet tells Death that there is no need to lecture this wise king on the impermanence of the world, as he already understands it completely through his profound wisdom.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,1.2],[1.2,1.4],[1.4,1.9],[1.9,2.76],[2.76,3.1],[3.1,3.35],[3.35,3.69],[3.69,4.03],[4.03,4.37],[4.6,5.25],[5.25,5.8],[5.8,6.3],[6.3,6.7],[6.7,7.8],[7.8,8.22],[8.22,8.59],[8.59,9.34],[9.34,9.9],[9.9,10.2],[10.2,10.5],[10.5,10.8],[10.8,12.3],[12.3,12.7],[12.7,13.34],[13.34,13.85],[13.85,14.9],[14.9,15.4],[15.53,15.86],[15.86,16.18],[16.18,17.26],[17.26,17.69],[17.69,18.34],[18.34,18.74],[18.74,19.04],[19.04,19.34],[19.71,20.57],[20.57,21.14],[21.14,21.62],[21.62,22.24],[22.2